From b0e121cefc262a5c641aa06e0677334515a73a9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:40:59 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] feat(edm): sinker electrode wear compensation in Z

A stated axial wear rate - a condition's `wear` in the .mch edm
condition table, or a wear measured on the op between burns (length
lost over depth burned, which wins) - deepens each burn layer by the
rate times the depth burned by then. With neither stated the burn is
not compensated and its path and page say so. A rate that is not a
finite ratio in [0, 1) is refused by name at the machine file and at
CreateOperation / EditOperationParams; every layer move is bounded by
the stated floor plus the compensation and an over-deep move refuses
by name. The stock sim judges the worn electrode's burn. Additive DTO
keys: older files load unchanged. Golden sinker_wear_layers.cl.

Fixes #546

